---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About ImageLabKit — Local-First Image, PDF & Graphics Studio"
  description="Learn how ImageLabKit delivers fast, verifiable browser-side image conversion, compression, PDF tools, barcode/QR generation, and AI OCR."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14 space-y-8 animate-fade-up">
    <header>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400 mb-2">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950">
        Built for Speed &amp; Verifiable Privacy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed">
        ImageLabKit is a browser-first image, PDF, text, and graphics studio built so anyone can
        convert, compress, merge, crop, redact, watermark, extract text, and prepare print-ready
        documents quickly without signups, daily paywalls, or intrusive clutter.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="studio-card rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Why Browser-First Architecture?</h2>
        <p>
          Traditional online converters upload your personal portraits, ID cards, handwritten
          signatures, invoices, and PDFs to remote servers and cap free users to a few tasks per
          day. By running WebAssembly image codecs (MozJPEG, LibWebP, UPNG) and native PDF engines
          directly inside background Web Workers, ImageLabKit keeps core utilities instant,
          unlimited, and strictly private on your device. For tasks requiring multimodal vision —
          such as bilingual English &amp; Bengali OCR — we use encrypted, zero-storage serverless
          processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Verify Zero Uploads Yourself</h2>
        <p>
          Open your browser’s <strong>DevTools → Network</strong> tab (press <code>F12</code>),
          clear the request log, and run any image conversion, compression, merge, passport sheet,
          crop, blur, EXIF cleanup, barcode/QR, or PDF tool on ImageLabKit. You will see zero file
          upload requests leaving your device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Testing &amp; Editorial Standards</h2>
        <p>
          Every utility and technical guide in our{' '}
          <a href="/guides" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-semibold hover:underline">Guides hub</a>{' '}
          is benchmarked across desktop and mobile browsers against real smartphone captures (JPG,
          PNG, WEBP, AVIF, and iOS HEIC) and multi-page PDF documents. We enforce magic-byte
          validation, memory-safe canvas caps, and clean, minimal interfaces with zero dark
          patterns.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Open-Source Technology Stack</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">
          ImageLabKit is built on trusted, permissive open-source libraries (MIT, Apache-2.0, and BSD):
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-zinc-600 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Astro, React, Tailwind CSS &amp; Lucide Icons</strong> — MIT / ISC licenses</li>
          <li><strong>@jsquash/jpeg (MozJPEG) &amp; @jsquash/webp (LibWebP)</strong> — Apache-2.0 / BSD licenses</li>
          <li><strong>UPNG.js, JSZip, jsPDF, pdf-lib, exifr, heic-to, JsBarcode &amp; qr-code-styling</strong> — MIT licenses</li>
          <li><strong>PDF.js (pdfjs-dist)</strong> — Apache-2.0 license</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
